{
  "title": "Queue names that become unrecognized after a catalog change for the AI name resolver",
  "description": "Unrecognized ingredient names reach ingredient_name_resolutions only on a write: recipe create/update or a shopping-list write. \
At startup, requeue_stale_keys only re-asks rows that are already resolved and whose catalog key stopped resolving. \
So when a resolver change makes a previously resolved name Unresolved, it is never asked about unless its recipe is edited. \
In #728, for example, 'cooked red lentils or cannellini beans' used to count as beans and is now deliberately unknown. \
Its calories stay unknown in prod even though the learned-name resolver could answer it. \
Fix: on startup (or behind a make target), enqueue every current recipe and shopping-list item name that the committed catalog and learned table both leave unresolved, then wake the worker. \
Add an e2e test.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 2,
